# Unit X Lecture X - Vibe Coding and AI Programming

Date: Oct 7, 2026

## Key Concepts

- Vibe coding is using AI to make code without really understanding the code.
- AI can write code quickly, but that does not mean the code is good.
- Code that runs can still be wrong.
- Testing is important when using AI-generated code.
- AI often creates more code than needed.
- Better prompts can improve the result.
- AI works better when it has many similar examples to learn from.
- AI should be used as a tool, not as a replacement for knowing how to program.

## What is Vibe Coding?

Vibe coding is when someone tells AI what they want and lets it create the code for them. If something breaks, they may just tell the AI to fix it instead of reading the code themselves.

The problem is that the person may not know what the AI changed or why something stopped working. This can make simple problems harder to fix later.

